diff --git a/.l9/integration-contract.yaml b/.l9/integration-contract.yaml
--- a/.l9/integration-contract.yaml
+++ b/.l9/integration-contract.yaml
@@ -177,3 +177,36 @@
     - minimum SDK requirements are explicit
     - exact SDK pinning is required for central CI
     - consumers must not infer compatibility from artifact shape alone
+
+ci_provider_invariants:
+  - id: L9-CI-SDK-001
+    statement: >-
+      For one exact repository snapshot the SDK must enumerate every supported applicable
+      language, framework and provider prerequisite; it must not collapse a mixed repository
+      into a single preferred language. Unsupported or uncertain detections must remain
+      visible.
+  - id: L9-CI-SDK-002
+    statement: >-
+      The SDK must distinguish applicability, planned selection, actual invocation,
+      completed execution, analyzed paths, explicit exclusions, failed steps and missing
+      evidence for each provider. Not-applicable requires evidence of nonapplicability;
+      skip, unsupported and unknown cannot become completed-pass.
+  - id: L9-CI-SDK-003
+    statement: >-
+      Every effective scanner rulepack is the reproducible composition of versioned SDK
+      baseline, applicable language/framework packs and authorized product-specific
+      restrictions. Resolve exact rule content/configuration digests; subordinate rules
+      cannot suppress the organization baseline, and mutable remote registry labels alone do
+      not prove reproducibility.
+  - id: L9-CI-SDK-004
+    statement: >-
+      Before consolidating or retiring any effective scanner rule or configuration, prove
+      its unique intended behavior with at least one known-bad trigger and known-good
+      nontrigger. Where equivalence is not proven, retain the scoped owner and report the
+      coverage gap.
+  - id: L9-CI-SDK-005
+    statement: >-
+      SDK observations preserve exact provider identity, original rule IDs, source revision,
+      report provenance, scope and failures. Deduplication may correlate findings but may
+      not erase a distinct native result, unsupported severity, independent source or unique
+      coverage; SDK emits no final Assurance verdict.
